<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stăgīra</span></b> ,
		ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στάγειρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Macedonia</i>, <i>the
				birthplace of Aristotle</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10,
				17, § 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 4,
			8</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stăgīrītes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σταγειρίτης</span>, <i>the Stagirite</i>, i.
			e. <i>Aristotle</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac.
				1, 4, 17</span></i>; also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stăgērītes</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 1, 3</span></i>.</div>
